torId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28620725752", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "International organization of esperanto speakers Headquartered in Universal Esperanto Association Main Office. Founded 1908.", "newValue": "The Universal Esperanto Association (UEA), founded in 1908, stands as a pivotal organization within the global movement for linguistic equality and international communication. Headquartered in Rotterdam, Netherlands, the UEA seeks to promote the Esperanto language, conceived by L. L. Zamenhof in 1887, as a universal second language that transcends national boundaries and cultural barriers. Its establishment coincided with a broader trend in the early 20th century that emphasized internationalism and cooperation, particularly in the wake of escalating nationalism and conflict across Europe.

